# Button

> Lede 0.7.1's docs for Button, installed with it. Setup, and every item in the release: [README.md](README.md). Online: https://lede.cloudcompute.com/reference/button.md

A native `<button>`, or an `<a>` when given `href`, in five variants. `buttonClass` gives an element of your own the same classes.

## Install

```bash
npx shadcn@latest add @lede/button
```

The command needs Lede's registry in `components.json`, as [README.md](README.md#use-it-in-a-shadcn-project) shows. It also installs the items [`lede-theme`](lede-theme.md) and [`lede-utils`](lede-utils.md). The item's JSON, with each file's source, is https://lede.cloudcompute.com/r/v0.7.1/button.json.

## Import

```tsx
import { Button } from '@/components/lede/button';
```

## Files and exports

| Installs to | Import from | Exports |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `components/lede/button.tsx` | `@/components/lede/button` | `buttonClass` (function), `Button` (component), `ButtonProps` (type) |

## Props

A native `<button>`, or a native `<a>` when given `href`. HTML attributes and `ref` go on that element.

| Prop | Type | Default | Description |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `variant` | `'filled' \| 'tinted' \| 'gray' \| 'plain' \| 'glass'` | `gray` | `'filled'` for the one prominent action, `'tinted'` for secondary emphasis, `'gray'` for the rest, `'plain'` for text only and `'glass'` over media. Default `'gray'`. |
| `size` | `'sm' \| 'md' \| 'lg'` |  |  |
| `shape` | `'capsule' \| 'rounded'` | `capsule` | Default `'capsule'`. |
| `tone` | `ToneSubset<'primary' \| 'critical'>` |  | `'critical'` for destructive actions. |
| `icon` | `React.ReactNode` |  | Inline SVG drawn in `currentColor`. With no children the control is square: give it `aria-label`. |
| `block` | `boolean` |  | Full width. |
| `ref` | `ButtonRef<HTMLButtonElement>` |  |  |

Button also takes the attributes of `<button>` or `<a>`, whichever it renders, such as `className`.

These props use types from other items:

- `ToneSubset<T extends Tone>` is `T`, declared in [`lede-utils`](lede-utils.md#types).

## Example

The smallest working use, from the docs site:

```tsx
import { Button } from '@/components/lede/button';

export function SaveBar({ onSave }: { onSave: () => void }) {
  return (
    <div>
      <Button variant="filled" onClick={onSave}>Save</Button>
      <Button variant="plain" href="/help/saving">Learn more</Button>
    </div>
  );
}
```

Docs: [Components](https://lede.cloudcompute.com/components.md).

